{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Take for yourself spices.</b> Those mentioned in the anointing oil — namely mor, sweet cane, cinnamon and cassia — and together with these, nataph, shechelet and chelbenah, and with them spices known for rectifying the aforementioned spices, as is known among apothecaries — that shebolet, for example, rectifies the reovarbivo, and salt-stone rectifies the agriko and their like. And our Sages of blessed memory received (Keritot 6a) that the rectifiers of the aforementioned spices are shebolet nerd, karkom and kosht." "<b>And pure frankincense.</b> Which requires no rectification. And so they are eleven spices that our Sages of blessed memory enumerated for the compounding of the incense."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "ריאוברביר\"ו and אגריק\"ו are transliterated as in the Hebrew, as they appear to be technical/pharmacological terms in medieval materia medica; they are left untranslated since their exact identification is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:38.323723033Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}